+### RLA auxiliary targets
+
+The action head can be given extra output-query tokens trained to regress the RLA autoencoder's
+latent actions, as an auxiliary objective alongside the action L1. It is off by default
+(`ARM=baseline`) and, when off, byte-identical to upstream. `ARM=rla` turns it on for both
+`train_libero.sh` and `run_libero_eval.sh`. Design and verified findings:
+[rla-vla-adapter.md](rla-vla-adapter.md); commands:
+[rla-vla-adapter-runbook.md](rla-vla-adapter-runbook.md).
+
